# Line endings, settled once and for all.
#
# text=auto: git stores LF in the repository and checks out the platform's
# native endings (CRLF on Windows). This cooperates with core.autocrlf=true
# instead of fighting it, so `git status` stays clean no matter which git
# config a machine happens to have.
#
# A previous attempt used "* -text" (store bytes verbatim). That preserved
# CRLF in the blobs, which conflicted with the system-level autocrlf=true and
# made two git processes on the SAME repo disagree about whether files were
# modified. text=auto is the conventional fix.
* text=auto

# Binary formats - never translate these, ever.
*.rom  binary
*.ROM  binary
*.bin  binary
*.sof  binary
*.pof  binary
*.jic  binary
*.zip  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.step binary
*.dat  binary
*.qws  binary
*.hex  binary
*.dsk  binary
